### 7.1 Cumulative History Expansion & Latency Scaling
In Step 1 of `qwen3_smoke_003`, the initial prompt was ~1,500 tokens. On hybrid CPU/GPU compute (34% CPU layers / 66% GPU layers on 4 GB VRAM), `qwen3:4b` completed prompt ingestion and generated `ClickActionModel(click=33)` in 102.9 seconds. In Step 2, `browser-use` appended the full previous step history, action result, and updated DOM tree, expanding context to >3,200 tokens. At hybrid ingestion rates (~15–20 tokens/sec), processing 3,200 tokens required >180 seconds, triggering the outer step watchdog ceiling.

### 7.2 In-Flight Cancellation Telemetry
In `browser-use`, step timeouts are enforced via:
```python
await asyncio.wait_for(self.step(step_info), timeout=self.settings.step_timeout)
```
When the 180-second timeout expires, `asyncio.wait_for` injects `asyncio.CancelledError`. In Python 3.8+, `CancelledError` inherits directly from `BaseException`, not `Exception`. In run 004, the wrapper's `except Exception:` handler was bypassed, resulting in empty telemetry (`model_call_telemetry: []`). 

In run 005, implementing dedicated `except asyncio.CancelledError:` safely captured:
- `call_index`: `1`, `status`: `"cancelled_in_flight"`, `error_type`: `"CancelledError"`.
- `wall_clock_seconds`: `179.6983s`.
- Unobserved server metrics (`prompt_tokens`, `eval_duration_ms`) were strictly preserved as `null`.

